// Core slice surface.
//
// Slices are compiler-managed views over contiguous storage. The concrete
// pointer/length carrier is intentionally private to the compiler/runtime
// handoff, but the semantic names that proofs and operators refer to should
// live here.
//
// Planned public surface:
// - Slice::Length ranks a slice by its current length for termination proofs.
// - index and subslice operators require bounds proofs before lowering to the
//   private descriptor primitive.
// - mutable views carry the same overlap and borrow obligations as their
//   source owner.
